    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a2">

                <pb facs="0788" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg774"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roux, collector, to
                        Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fernandina, Florida</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi>
                        29, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Respectfully referring to your letter of
                    the 22d March instant, I have the honor to reply—</p>
                <p>That there is no steamer in or near these waters named Salvador, nor any steamer
                    else than small tow-boats employed hereabout.</p>
                <pb facs="0789" n="775" xml:id="pg775"/>
                <p>Should any movement be developed, your instructions relative to the neutrality
                    act of April 20, 1818, will be duly enforced.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. ROUX.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury, Washington, D.
                        C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
